parameters.content:
## 1. Start and configure

Run the workflow manually while testing or let it run every six hours after validation.

Edit only **Configure opportunity agent** to set:
- public RSS feed URLs, one per line;
- include, priority, and exclusion keywords;
- the score threshold;
- the Gmail review recipient;
- the OpenRouter model;
- truthful profile context for the draft.

Keep API keys in n8n credentials, never in this node.

## 3. Score and filter

Each RSS item is cleaned and scored with visible rules:
- topic keyword: +8;
- priority or buying-intent keyword: +10;
- exclusion keyword: -30.

The score stays between 0 and 100. Only items at or above **minimumScore** continue to OpenRouter. Lower-scoring items return to the feed loop without generating an AI call, which controls cost and noise.

parameters.jsCode:
const config = $input.first().json;
const urls = String(config.rssUrls || '').split(/\r?\n|,/).map(value => value.trim()).filter(value => /^https?:\/\//i.test(value));
return urls.map(rssUrl => ({ json: { ...config, rssUrl } }));

const config = $('Configure opportunity agent').first().json;
const include = String(config.includeKeywords || '').split(',').map(v => v.trim().toLowerCase()).filter(Boolean);
const priority = String(config.priorityKeywords || '').split(',').map(v => v.trim().toLowerCase()).filter(Boolean);
const exclude = String(config.excludeKeywords || '').split(',').map(v => v.trim().toLowerCase()).filter(Boolean);
const clean = value => String(value || '').replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/&amp;/gi, '&').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
const rows = $input.all().map(item => item.json || {});
return rows.flatMap(row => {
  const title = clean(row.title);
  const url = String(row.link || row.guid || '').trim();
  if (!title || !/^https?:\/\//i.test(url)) return [];
  const description = clean(row.content || row.contentSnippet || row.description || row.summary).slice(0, 12000);
  const haystack = `${title} ${description}`.toLowerCase();
  const includeHits = include.filter(word => haystack.includes(word));
  const priorityHits = priority.filter(word => haystack.includes(word));
  const excludeHits = exclude.filter(word => haystack.includes(word));
  const score = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, 20 + includeHits.length * 8 + priorityHits.length * 10 - excludeHits.length * 30));
  return [{ json: { title, url, description, publishedAt: row.isoDate || row.pubDate || '', score, scoreReasons: [...includeHits.map(v => `topic: ${v}`), ...priorityHits.map(v => `intent: ${v}`), ...excludeHits.map(v => `excluded: ${v}`)], sourceFeed: config.rssUrl, reviewEmail: config.reviewEmail, minimumScore: config.minimumScore, openRouterModel: config.openRouterModel, candidateProfile: config.candidateProfile } }];
});

